  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 243 AM MDT Sun Oct 11 2026\n\nOn Wednesday and Thursday, the upper-level pattern is forecast \nto remain southwesterly and mover over the area from the Four \nCorners region. A shortwave is forecast to move over the area \novernight Wednesday and into Thursday morning. Guidance favors \nthe shortwave to pass through before midnight Thursday morning. \nWith this passage and mid- to low-level moisture being \ntransported from the southwest, chances for widespread showers \nWednesday and throughout Thursday are medium to high (50-75%) \nonce the shortwave passes. There is higher confidence that \nshowers will happen on Wednesday night.\n\nOn Friday and Saturday, it becomes a little less clear as the \noverall pattern shifts from southwesterly to northwesterly flow.\nAs of now, the upper-level trough pattern is forecast to merge \nwith the secondary trough system to the north of the area and \nslides east. With that being said, there is medium confidence \n(45%) that this will lead to a dry cold front to pass through \nthe area from the northwest Friday. Temperatures are expected to\nbe in the 50s and slightly build back up into the 60s on \nSaturday with both days having scattered clouds. There are hints\nthat guidance is favoring a slower trough progression, keeping \nit within the area. This may cause slightly more warmer \ntemperatures for each day being roughly 10 degrees more.",
